CORE
trap.sh
--resolve-dynamic-sites --show-dynamic-sites
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^shell-trap:trap.sh:7:1: .*: \{ ":", "done=yes" \}$
^shell-trap:trap.sh:9:1: .*: \{ "rm -f ", "rm -f "\*"tmp\."\* \}$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The action of a trap on EXIT is a dynamic site. A text with an unknown
part, such as a file name from mktemp, is a template; by the
specification of mktemp, its name ends in tmp. and letters and digits, or
is empty where mktemp fails.
